### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:9090
@token = paste_token_here_after_login

### ==========================================
### STEP 0: Setup — Register and Login
### ==========================================

### 0.1 Register a test user
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test Admin",
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "secret123"
}

### 0.2 Login (copy the token from response and paste it in @token above)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "secret123"
}

### ==========================================
### AUTHORS — CHECK constraints
### ==========================================

### 1. Empty name (should be rejected)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/authors
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": ""
}

### Expected: 500 (CHECK authors_name_not_blank)
### Server log: "violates check constraint authors_name_not_blank"

### 2. Whitespace-only name (should be rejected — trim() makes it empty)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/authors
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "   "
}

### Expected: 500 (same constraint — length(trim(name)) = 0)

### 3. Name longer than 100 characters (should be rejected)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/authors
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA"
}

### Expected: 500 (VARCHAR(100) overflow)

### 4. Create a valid author
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/authors
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "George Orwell"
}

### Expected: 201 Created

### 5. Same author name in lowercase (case-insensitive unique — should be rejected)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/authors
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "george orwell"
}

### Expected: 500 (UNIQUE INDEX authors_name_unique)
### Server log: "duplicate key value violates unique constraint authors_name_unique"

### 6. Same author name in UPPERCASE (case-insensitive unique — should be rejected)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/authors
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "GEORGE ORWELL"
}

### Expected: 500 (same INDEX)

### ==========================================
### USERS — CHECK constraints
### ==========================================

### 7. Register with empty name (should be rejected)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "",
  "email": "test1@example.com",
  "password": "secret123"
}

### Expected: 400 (handler DTO validation is first line of defense — required)

### 8. Register with uppercase email (should be rejected — CHECK users_email_lowercase)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test User 2",
  "email": "TEST2@example.com",
  "password": "secret123"
}

### Expected: 500 (CHECK users_email_lowercase)
### Server log: "violates check constraint users_email_lowercase"
### Note: This means the app is NOT lowercasing email yet — that is the next step (normalization)

### 9. Register with duplicate email (should be rejected — UNIQUE email)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Another User",
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "secret123"
}

### Expected: 409 Conflict (handler maps error code 23505 to 409)

### ==========================================
### BOOKS — CHECK constraints
### ==========================================

### 10. Book with empty title (should be rejected)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/books
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "",
  "release_year": 1949,
  "author_id": 1
}

### Expected: 500 (CHECK books_title_not_blank)

### 11. Book with year 0 (should be rejected)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/books
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Test Book",
  "release_year": 0,
  "author_id": 1
}

### Expected: 500 (CHECK books_year_valid — 0 is not BETWEEN 1000 AND 2100)

### 12. Book with year 99999 (should be rejected)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/books
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Test Book 2",
  "release_year": 99999,
  "author_id": 1
}

### Expected: 500 (CHECK books_year_valid)

### 13. Book with non-existent author_id (FK violation — should be rejected)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/books
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Test Book 3",
  "release_year": 1949,
  "author_id": 9999
}

### Expected: 400 Bad Request (handler maps error code 23503 to ErrInvalidAuthor -> 400)

### 14. Create a valid book
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/books
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "1984",
  "release_year": 1949,
  "author_id": 1
}

### Expected: 201 Created

### 15. Same book with same author (composite unique — should be rejected)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/books
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "1984",
  "release_year": 1949,
  "author_id": 1
}

### Expected: 500 (UNIQUE books_title_author_unique)
### Server log: "duplicate key value violates unique constraint books_title_author_unique"

### ==========================================
### FOREIGN KEY — ON DELETE RESTRICT
### ==========================================

### 16. Try to delete an author who still has books (should be rejected)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/authors/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Expected: 409 Conflict (handler maps error code 23503 to ErrAuthorHasBooks -> 409)